{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.TrivialWitness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.TrivialWitness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Monoidal.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.CategoryTheory.Coherence","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TrivialWitness.nonempty_quantumUniverse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TrivialWitness.nonempty_quantumUniverse","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean#L125-L130","doc":"**`QuantumUniverse` is inhabited** — the claim `quantum-universe-exists.lean`\ncarries as an `axiom`, now a theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TrivialWitness.trivialQU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TrivialWitness.trivialQU","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean#L97-L123","doc":"**The trivial quantum universe.**  `C = ModuleCat R`, `A = 𝟙`, one block.\n\nDischarges every field, including the five added under `qou-w1g8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TrivialWitness.unitFrobHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TrivialWitness.unitFrobHopf","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean#L63-L95","doc":"**The Frobenius–Hopf object at the tensor unit.**\n\n`μ = λ_`, `Δ = λ_⁻¹`, everything else the identity, `coev = λ_⁻¹`.  Every\nequation is pure coherence and holds in *any* monoidal category — including\nthe eight algebra / coalgebra / antipode laws added 2026-09-14 under bean\n`qou-c64q`, which is the point of keeping this witness: it is the only\nrecord-literal construction of `FrobeniusHopfData` in the corpus, so it is\nthe only thing that can falsify a newly-added field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TrivialWitness.unitEndEquivModuleCat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TrivialWitness.unitEndEquivModuleCat","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/TrivialWitness.lean#L41-L61","doc":"**`End(𝟙)` is the ground ring**, for `ModuleCat R`.\n\n`r ↦ r • 𝟙` with inverse `f ↦ f(1)`.  This is the `unitEndEquiv` obligation,\nand it holds over any commutative ring — no field needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}